# C ⊑ D via Chain(t,u) ⊑ r + Range(r,F): the chain-materialised r-edge's
# target must be F, and C already has ∃t.∃u.F ⊑ D, so C ⊑ D. HermiT confirms
# this pair; Konclude under-reports it (a further under-report instance, not
# a disagreement between the two peers).
#
# NOTE: this crate's own `build_model` REFUSES this fixture outright
# (Err(ChainRangeOutOfProfile) — see §4 of the design spec: a chain-implied
# super-role paired with a range is out of this instrument's profile), so the
# acceptance invariant holds here trivially regardless of this oracle's
# content. Recorded anyway per the "one oracle per fixture" contract, and
# because Phase 2's chain/range fold is expected to make this fixture
# buildable — at which point this oracle becomes load-bearing.
provenance: hermit   # Konclude also under-reports this pair
subclass: C D
